# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# kernel-slim-typec.config: Type-C + DisplayPort alt mode delta on slim K3.
#
# Merged on top of ~/android/build/k3-slim/.config (branch
# instantnoodlep-k3-slim-typec in ~/src/l-k3-typec) with
# scripts/kconfig/merge_config.sh -m + olddefconfig, built with
# O=~/android/build/k3-slim-typec. See TYPEC-DP-PLAN.md for the port and
# the gated runbook.
#
# The Type-C stack is built in (=y), not a module, on purpose: with
# dr_mode = "otg" dwc3 waits for the usb-role-switch, so the PM8150B
# port/PD PHY, TCPM, the FSA4480 mux and the DP altmode driver must be
# present at boot for the gadget role (and the owner's USB networking)
# to come up without depending on module load order. Already set in the
# slim config and left untouched: TYPEC=y, USB_ROLE_SWITCH=y,
# USB_DWC3_DUAL_ROLE=y, PHY_QCOM_QMP_COMBO=y, DRM_MSM_DP=y, USB_HID=y.
# Charger drivers stay out (POWER-M5-PLAN P2b owner gate); nothing here
# changes a charge limit.

# --- Identify the build ---
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-instantnoodlep-k3-slim-typec"

# --- Type-C stack, built in ---
CONFIG_TYPEC_TCPM=y
CONFIG_TYPEC_QCOM_PMIC=y
CONFIG_TYPEC_MUX_FSA4480=y
CONFIG_TYPEC_DP_ALTMODE=y
